## Optional Polish (only if you want it)

### 1. Animator Controllers
Any script that calls `GetComponent<Animator>()` (PlayerController, EnemyAI) will log a warning if no Animator is attached.

**Fix:**
1. Create an Animator Controller in `Assets/Animations/` (**right-click → Create → Animator Controller**).
2. Select the Player (or Enemy) GameObject in the Scene.
3. Add an **Animator** component and assign your new controller to its **Controller** slot.
4. Add the animation states your script triggers:
{% for script in scripts %}
{% if script.type == "player" %}
   - Player animations: `Speed` (float), `Jump` (trigger) — used by `{{ script.name }}.cs`
{% endif %}
{% if script.type == "enemy" %}
   - Enemy animations: `Speed` (float), `Attack` (trigger), `Death` (trigger) — used by `{{ script.name }}.cs`
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if "animation_rigging" in features %}

> **Animation Rigging** is included in this project. After adding an Animator, add a **Rig Builder** component and set up IK rigs for limb targeting.
{% endif %}

{% if "cinemachine" in features %}
### 2. Cinemachine Camera (optional upgrade)

The built-in follow camera already works. For a more polished rig, **Cinemachine** is included:
1. Add a **Cinemachine Virtual Camera** (`GameObject → Cinemachine → Virtual Camera`).
2. Set **Follow** and **Look At** to the Player Transform.
3. Tune **Body** (Framing Transposer / 3rd Person Follow) and **Aim** settings.
{% endif %}
{% if "navmesh" in features %}

### 3. NavMesh Bake

`EnemyAI.cs` uses **NavMeshAgent** for pathfinding. The agent will log errors until the NavMesh is baked.

**Fix:**
1. Mark all static geometry as **Navigation Static** (Inspector → Static dropdown).
2. Open **Window → AI → Navigation**.
3. Go to the **Bake** tab and click **Bake**.
{% endif %}
{% if "audio" in features and "audio_manager" in scripts | map(attribute="type") | list %}

### 4. Audio Clips (optional)

The **AudioManager** and its AudioSources are already wired in the scene. To add sound, drop AudioClips into `Assets/Audio/` and assign them on the AudioManager in the Inspector (`mainTheme` / `sfxClips`).
{% endif %}
{% if "networking" in features %}

### 8. Networking Setup

**Netcode for GameObjects** is included. To enable multiplayer:
1. Add a **NetworkManager** component to the GameManager GameObject.
2. Assign the **Network Prefabs** list (your Player prefab must have a `NetworkObject` component).
3. Implement `NetworkBehaviour` on any synced scripts instead of `MonoBehaviour`.
{% endif %}
{% if "addressables" in features %}

### 9. Addressables

**Addressables** is included. To use asset streaming:
1. Open **Window → Asset Management → Addressables → Groups**.
2. Mark Prefabs and large assets as Addressable.
3. Build the Addressables catalog before making a build.
{% endif %}

